  Telemetry v3: Event-Level Storage with DuckDB Implementation Plan

  For Claude: REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.

  Goal: Restore event-level telemetry granularity using DuckDB to query JSONL files directly, enabling rich charts and session timeline visualization.

  Architecture: Enhanced hooks write events to session JSONL files with agent_type, workflow_id, and workflow_phase context. Session-end hook compresses old files. DuckDBStore queries both raw and gzipped
  JSONL files. Charts.py uses DuckDBStore for SQL-based chart generation.

  Tech Stack: Python, DuckDB (already in project), gzip, existing hooks infrastructure, existing JSONL session logs.

  ---
  Overview

  The design document (enhanced_telemetry) specifies 5 work items:
  1. Enhance telemetry hooks - Tag events with agent_type, workflow_id, workflow_phase
  2. Add session-end compression hook - Gzip JSONL files when session closes
  3. Extend DuckDBStore - Add query methods for the 6 charts
  4. Update charts.py - Use DuckDBStore instead of JSON telemetry file
  5. Build session timeline UI - Interactive narrative explorer

  This plan implements items 1-4. Item 5 (timeline UI) is a separate follow-on task.

